    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21759" root="شجع" body-key="$">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَجِعٌ</span></b> ; fem. with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ة</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شُجَاعٌ</span>, in three places.
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَجِعُ القَوَائِمِ</span> <i>Quick in the shifting of the legs,</i>
applied to a he-camel; and so <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَجِعَةٌ</span> and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَجْعَآءُ</span></b> ,
applied to a she-camel. (S, K.) And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَوَائِمُ شَجِعَاتٌ</span>
<i>Quick, and light, active,</i> or <i>nimble, legs.</i> (TA.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <i>Mad,</i> applied to a camel. (Ibn-'Abbád, K.)

